	[
		'slug'        => 'builders-clean-vs-sparkle-clean',
		'title'       => 'Builders Clean vs Sparkle Clean: What’s the Difference?',
		'seo_title'   => 'Builders Clean vs Sparkle Clean: What’s the Difference?',
		'description' => 'Builders clean vs sparkle clean explained: what each stage covers, when to book them and which one you need after renovation work in Hull or East Yorkshire.',
		'category'    => 'after-builders',
		'service'     => 'after-builders-cleaning',
		'related'     => [ 'cleaning-after-home-improvements', 'removing-paint-and-plaster-dust', 'protect-home-during-renovation' ],
		'image'       => 'new build interior',
		'excerpt'     => 'A builders clean gets a site tidy and safe; a sparkle clean makes it ready to live in. Here’s what each covers and which your project needs.',
		'content'     => <<<'HTML'
<p>A builders clean is the first, rougher clean once construction work finishes: removing debris, heavy dust and obvious mess so the site is safe and ready for final checks. A sparkle clean is the final, detailed clean just before handover or moving in, leaving every surface dust-free, polished and ready to use.</p>
<p>Both terms come from the construction industry, where they're often priced and booked as separate stages. For homeowners, landlords and businesses in Hull and East Yorkshire the distinction matters, because quotes can use either term and it's easy to pay for one while expecting the other.</p>
<div class="cc-takeaways"><p class="cc-takeaways__title">Key takeaways</p><ul><li>A builders clean, or rough clean, removes debris and heavy dust straight after the main works.</li><li>A sparkle clean is the final, detailed clean that makes a space ready to live in, let, sell or open.</li><li>Larger projects usually need both, in that order, with snagging work in between.</li><li>Always check what a quote includes rather than relying on the name alone.</li></ul></div>
<h2>What is a builders clean?</h2>
<p>A builders clean, sometimes called a rough clean or initial clean, happens once the main construction work is complete, often while some trades are still finishing off. Its job is to turn a building site into a clean, safe shell.</p>
<p>It typically covers:</p>
<ul>
<li>Clearing loose debris, packaging and small offcuts (bulk waste and skips are usually the builder's responsibility)</li>
<li>Vacuuming heavy dust from floors, sills and ledges with an industrial vacuum</li>
<li>A first wipe of surfaces, doors and frames</li>
<li>Removing the worst plaster splashes and adhesive spots</li>
<li>Making walkways clear and safe for inspections and remaining trades</li>
</ul>
<p>Some builders carry out this stage themselves, others bring in a cleaning company. Either way, a builders clean isn't designed to leave a space ready to live in. Fine dust will still be settling, protective films are usually left on, and the insides of cupboards and appliances won't have been touched.</p>
<h2>What is a sparkle clean?</h2>
<p>The sparkle clean, also called the final clean or handover clean, is the detailed finish. It's carried out once every trade has gone and snagging is complete, so nothing brings fresh dust in afterwards. It typically includes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Every surface dusted and wiped from ceiling to floor, including light fittings, switches, sockets and radiators</li>
<li>Insides of cupboards, drawers, wardrobes and appliances</li>
<li>Protective films, stickers and labels removed from windows, appliances and fittings</li>
<li>Glass and mirrors polished streak-free</li>
<li>Grout haze removed from tiles, and bathroom fittings polished</li>
<li>Remaining paint, plaster and sealant marks carefully removed</li>
<li>Hard floors vacuumed and mopped, often more than once, and carpets thoroughly vacuumed</li>
</ul>
<p>For most homeowners, what they picture when they book an <a href="{{service:after-builders-cleaning}}">after builders clean</a> is really a sparkle clean. Our guide to <a href="{{guide:cleaning-after-home-improvements}}">what's included in an after builders clean</a> goes through it room by room.</p>
<h2>Builders clean vs sparkle clean: side-by-side comparison</h2>
<table>
<thead><tr><th></th><th>Builders clean</th><th>Sparkle clean</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>When</td><td>Straight after the main works, before snagging</td><td>After all trades and snagging are finished</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purpose</td><td>Make the site safe, tidy and ready for final work</td><td>Make the space ready to live in, let, sell or open</td></tr>
<tr><td>Level of detail</td><td>Heavy dust and debris, first wipe of surfaces</td><td>Every surface, inside and out, with a polished finish</td></tr>
<tr><td>Dust</td><td>Bulk dust removed</td><td>Fine settled dust removed, with repeat passes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Protective films</td><td>Usually left on</td><td>Removed</td></tr>
<tr><td>Inside cupboards and appliances</td><td>Not usually</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ready to move in?</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h2>Do you need both a builders clean and a sparkle clean?</h2>
<p>It depends on the size and type of the job.</p>
<h3>Small projects</h3>
<p>After decorating, a new bathroom or a small kitchen refit, one detailed clean at the end is usually enough. Your builder tidies up and sweeps, then a professional sparkle clean follows.</p>
<h3>Extensions, loft conversions and full refurbishments</h3>
<p>Bigger projects benefit from both. A builders clean after the main works makes snagging easier to spot and stops dust being trodden through the rest of the house. The sparkle clean at the end delivers the finish. On large jobs, a light follow-up visit a week or so later catches dust that's still settling.</p>
<h3>New builds and commercial fit-outs</h3>
<p>Developers, shopfitters and office refurbishments almost always separate the two stages, and the sparkle clean is often timed for the day before handover. We handle these through our <a href="{{service:commercial-cleaning}}">commercial cleaning</a> service, and our guide to <a href="{{guide:choosing-a-commercial-cleaning-company}}">choosing a commercial cleaning contractor</a> covers the questions to ask.</p>
<div class="cc-callout"><p><strong>Tip:</strong> The less dust escapes during the build, the quicker both cleans will be. Our guide to <a href="{{guide:protect-home-during-renovation}}">protecting your home from dust during renovation</a> has practical steps you can agree with your builder before work starts.</p></div>
<h2>Which clean are you being quoted for?</h2>
<p>Terms vary between companies, so focus on the scope rather than the label. Before you accept a quote, ask:</p>
<ol>
<li>Are the insides of cupboards, drawers and appliances included?</li>
<li>Will protective films, stickers and labels be removed?</li>
<li>Are paint splashes, plaster marks and grout haze included, and on which surfaces?</li>
<li>Are windows cleaned inside only, or inside and out?</li>
<li>Is a follow-up visit included if dust resettles?</li>
<li>Is waste removal included, or is that the builder's job?</li>
</ol>
<p>We agree a fixed quote with a clear list of what's included before any work starts, so you know exactly which clean you're paying for. Splashes and residue are often the slowest part of a sparkle clean; our guide to <a href="{{guide:removing-paint-and-plaster-dust}}">removing plaster dust and paint splashes</a> explains why they take time to do safely.</p>
<h2>Builders and sparkle cleans for landlords and sellers</h2>
<p>If you're refurbishing a rental between tenancies, the sparkle clean effectively sets the standard for the next tenant, and it's the condition your check-in inventory will record. Our guide to <a href="{{guide:void-property-cleaning}}">void property cleaning</a> covers how to keep that turnaround short. Buying a newly renovated home yourself? A <a href="{{service:move-in-cleaning}}">move-in clean</a> gets it ready before your furniture arrives.</p>
<p>Selling after a renovation is another common reason to book a sparkle clean, because new work looks its best in listing photos and at viewings when it's spotless. Our tips on <a href="{{guide:cleaning-before-selling-your-house}}">cleaning before selling your house</a> cover the rest of the property.</p>
<h2>After builders cleaning across Hull and East Yorkshire</h2>
<p>Our team carries out builders cleans and sparkle cleans for homeowners, landlords, builders and businesses in <a href="{{area:hull}}">Hull</a>, <a href="{{area:hessle}}">Hessle</a>, <a href="{{area:brough}}">Brough</a> and across East Yorkshire. Our cleaners are insured and DBS-checked, bring their own equipment, and we're open seven days a week, which helps when a handover date is tight.</p>
<p>Find out more about our <a href="{{service:after-builders-cleaning}}">after builders cleaning service</a>, or <a href="{{page:contact}}">contact us</a> with your project dates and we'll recommend the right clean, or combination of cleans, for the job.</p>
